    pageItem P686_ITEMSPEC (
        type: popupLov
        label {
            label: Item Specification
        }
        lov {
            type: sqlQuery
            sqlQuery:
                ```sql
                Select nvl(sp.ItemSpecificationName, a.ItemSpecificationCode) d,
                       a.ItemSpecificationCode r
                  From IssueRegister a
                  Left Join ItemSpecification sp
                         On sp.ItemSpecificationCode = a.ItemSpecificationCode
                 Where a.ItemSpecificationCode Is Not Null
                   And (:P686_ITEM Is Null Or a.ItemCode = :P686_ITEM)
                   And ((Select GetUserPanelAB_apex() From dual) Is Null
                        Or (Select i9.Panel From Issue i9 Where i9.Tno = a.Tno)
                           = (Select GetUserPanelAB_apex() From dual))
                 Group By a.ItemSpecificationCode, sp.ItemSpecificationName
                 Order By 1
                ```
            displayExtraValues: false
            nullDisplayValue: All specifications
        }
        cascadingLov {
            parentItems: P686_ITEM
            itemsToSubmit: P686_ITEM
        }
        layout {
            sequence: 40
            region: @filter-drawer
            slot: regionBody
            columnSpan: 12
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/optional-above
            templateOptions: [
                #DEFAULT#
                t-Form-fieldContainer--stretchInputs
            ]
        }
        security {
            encryptSessionState: false
        }
        help {
            helpText: Narrowed by the Item filter when one is set, because a specification only means something under its item and the full list runs to 394. NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS - the rationale lives here rather than as a comment above the LOV query because an APEX list of values must begin with SELECT. A leading comment makes the item fail at render with "Error during rendering of page item", and apex validate passes it clean. Same fault was fixed on P690_LOCATION and repeated here.
        }
    )

